Article 2 (Application for Registration)
(1) An application submitted to the Minister of Justice pursuant to Article 2 (2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Legal Aid Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Decree") shall include the following:
1. Name;
2. Purpose;
3. Locations of the principal office and branch offices;
4. Names and addresses of officers;
5. Date of establishment.
(2) The following documents shall be attached to an application under paragraph (1): <Amended on May 31, 2010; Mar. 11, 2019; Feb. 7, 2022>
1. Articles of incorporation;
2. Résumés and written consents to appointment of officers;
3. A business plan and budgets for revenue and expenditures for the next two years;
4. The following documents certifying ownership of assets required to provide legal aid under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Decree:
(a) A copy of a lease contract (limited to cases that cannot be verified through a certified copy of the real estate register);
(b) A certificate of deposit balance or other documents certifying ownership of monetary assets that can actually be used as operating funds for legal aid activities;
5. Documents certifying attorney-at-law qualifications or other qualifications of officers and persons directly engaged in legal aid activities;
6. Deleted. <Apr. 17, 2023>
(3) Upon receipt of an application under paragraph (1), the responsible public official shall verify the contents of the following documents through shared use of administrative information under Article 36 (1) of the Electronic Government Act; provided, if the applicant or relevant officer does not consent to verification, the official shall require the documents to be attached: <Amended on May 31, 2010; Mar. 11, 2019; Apr. 17, 2023>
1. Certificate of corporate registration;
2. Certified copy of the real estate register certifying ownership of assets necessary for legal aid under Article 2 (1) 2 of the Decree;
3. Abstract of an officer's resident registration record (excluding the latter portion of the resident registration number).
